mechaber.en:
Workers — if their work is in the city, twice a week; and if their work is in another city, once a week.

{Rama: And some say if they do not sleep every night in their homes — their onah is once in eight days (Tur and Tosafot in name of R' Yoel bar Baruch).}

Donkey-drivers — once a week; camel-drivers — once in thirty days; sailors — once in six months. Torah scholars — their onah is once a week; and the way of Torah scholars is to use their bed from Friday night to Friday night.

A wife may restrain her husband from going to trade except to a nearby place so he will not deprive her of onah; and he may not go without her permission.

{Rama: And even if she gives him permission — he may not delay more than one month away and one month in his home (Tur and Rosh).}

And likewise she may restrain him from work whose onah is close to work whose onah is far — such as a donkey-driver who wishes to become a camel-driver, or a camel-driver who wishes to become a sailor. Torah scholars go out to Torah study without their wives' permission for two or three years.

{Rama: And likewise a traveler who became a Torah scholar — his wife cannot restrain him.}

If she gives him permission — a Torah scholar may travel as far as she permits (Tur in name of Raavad).
